# Concept D — Tree Hierarchy ★ chosen

Single wider panel. Projects collapsible; tasks render as children inline. **View switcher** lives at bottom of panel — dropdown so future views (Feed, Hybrid, etc.) plug in.

## Behavior

- Sidebar `w-64`
- Each project = collapsible row w/ chevron
- Expand → tasks listed beneath, indented
- Click project name → select project (kanban view)
- Click task → open task tab
- Multi-select projects can be expanded simultaneously
- Footer same as today (settings, usage, etc.) but laid out horizontally
- **Bottom: view-switcher button → dropdown menu of available sidebar views**

## View Switcher

Persistent button at bottom of sidebar. Shows current view name + caret. Click → dropdown lists views. Selected view persisted in `settings.sidebar_view`.

```
─────────────────────────
  [≡  Tree view  ▾]   ← view switcher
─────────────────────────
```

Dropdown open:

```
─────────────────────────
  ┌──────────────────┐
  │ ✓ Tree view      │  ← current
  │   Projects rail  │  ← classic w-18 icon rail
  │   (more soon…)   │
  └──────────────────┘
  [≡  Tree view  ▾]
─────────────────────────
```

Future views slot in same dropdown w/o redesign — registry pattern, each entry = `{ id, label, icon, component }`.

