## Implementation Notes

- Add `sidebar_view` to settings (string, default `'projects'` for backwards compat)
- Create `SidebarViewRegistry` — list of view defs `{ id, label, icon, render }`
- `AppSidebar` reads current view, picks renderer; ViewSwitcher always rendered at bottom
- Width adapts per view: `'projects' → w-18`, `'tree' → w-64`, future flex
- Zen mode (`!w-0`) overrides regardless of view
- Window-drag region (`h-10` top) preserved across all views

## Pros

- Single panel — minimal visual chunking
- Tree natural for hierarchy
- Easy global scanning of all work
- Search at top scopes globally
- View switcher = clean extensibility for future modes

## Cons

- Loses iconic project rail unless user opts back into it (still available)
- Long lists scroll a lot
- Reordering projects vs tasks UX must distinguish levels
- Footer icons need horizontal layout in wide views, vertical in narrow rail

